                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15582513" author="jongyoul" created="Mon, 17 Oct 2016 15:17:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=kavinkumarks&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;kavinkumarks&quot;&gt;kavinkumarks&lt;/a&gt; I think you may be confused interpreter group and interpreter. For your understanding, you should know the &apos;InterpreterGroup&apos; and &apos;interpreter&apos;. What people say SparkInterpreter means all of Spark*Interpreter including SparkInterpreter, SparkSqlInterpreter and so on. Thus correctly should we call &quot;InterpreterGroup&quot;. but in general, people calls it to SparkInterpreter becuase SparkInterpreter is a default interpreter of SparkInterpreter group. The default Interpreter what I told you means actually default &apos;InterpreterGroup&apos; name. If you use `%spark`, that means internally `%spark.spark`. Thus, your first screenshot means `md` is a default interpreter gorup in that note, and the second screenshot means Alluxio interpreter group has only one interpreter in this group name alluxio. Thus if you use `%alluxio`, that means as same as `%alluxio.alluxio&apos;. Thus that&apos;s the normal situation. BTW, I also agree to have it confused.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15584513" author="kavinkumarks" created="Tue, 18 Oct 2016 05:28:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=jongyoul&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;jongyoul&quot;&gt;jongyoul&lt;/a&gt; Thanks for the information and I got it.But what does &apos;default&apos; refer in the Interpreter page (which was about alluxio in the screenshot)? Will it be the default interpreter used for any note?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks,&lt;br/&gt;
Kavin&lt;br/&gt;
MailTo: kavin.kumar@imaginea.com&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15584992" author="jongyoul" created="Tue, 18 Oct 2016 09:26:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think that message looks wrong. Let me check&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
